WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.970
- All right everybody
let's finish up this hour,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.580
with something positive and inspiring.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.780
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.730
So street wear has become a
force in the fashion industry,

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.520
with billions spent on
the latest sneaker trends.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.850
But many believe that
there's a lack of plus size

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.260
representation in that market.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.350
And that's where Essie
from New York comes in.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.160
She co-founded a community
called Thick Laces.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.460
Which promotes street wear
among plus size women.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.803
Everybody say hi to Essie.

00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:29.227
(audience cheers)

00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:30.420
- [Kelly] Hi Essie.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.760
So how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.690
- So I've always been a
huge fan of street wear

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.550
and sneakers and things like that.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.707
And like everyone else
during the pandemic,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.590
other people picked up
baking banana bread.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.107
I picked up buying tons of sneakers.

00:00:46.107 --> 00:00:46.940
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.530
And so I was using hashtags,

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.490
and tagging these brands
that had the sneakers.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:53.430
And I was realizing,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.430
not only were they not featuring
women who look like me,

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.700
but they weren't featuring
any plus size women.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.630
And so I reached out to my best friend,

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.830
Katie who's the co-founder of Thick Laces.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.758
And I said,

00:01:03.758 --> 00:01:05.100
" Hey, we need to start
a community of our own.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.050
Because I see my timeline.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.860
I see women all the time who are plus size

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.550
and they are killing it and
they deserve to be seen."

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.320
And so we started Thick Laces.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.110
And it has quickly grown,

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.480
into something bigger
than we ever imagined.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.290
We got the chance to work with Reebok.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.558
We've worked with New Balance,

00:01:21.558 --> 00:01:22.391
and Nike,

00:01:22.391 --> 00:01:23.224
and eBay.

00:01:23.224 --> 00:01:24.057
And it's a community,

00:01:24.057 --> 00:01:25.550
that's really making a
change within the street wear

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.210
and sneaker community.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.739
So I'm so excited to continue the work.

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:31.850
- Well, what's incredible about this,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.940
is this isn't your first time to create

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.539
an online community, right?

00:01:35.539 --> 00:01:36.968
- It is not.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:40.038
I believe that representation
is super important.

00:01:40.038 --> 00:01:42.740
I grew up in the foster care system.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.499
And was later adopted
by a wonderful family.

00:01:45.499 --> 00:01:47.200
But in my younger years,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.700
being in the foster care system,

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.070
and also being plus size,

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.470
I never felt like I fit in.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.610
And so that's something
that stuck with me,

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.910
until I moved to New York City

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.490
to pursue a career in
fashion and modeling.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.580
And I was wearing these crop tops

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.130
and bright colors and all
these different things.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.027
And there were so many
plus size women saying,

00:02:05.027 --> 00:02:06.890
"I wish I could wear that."

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.060
And so I started the
hashtag golden confidence,

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.880
as a way for other women to use it

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.713
outside of myself,

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:14.410
to see like I'm wearing it.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.243
They're wearing it.

00:02:15.243 --> 00:02:16.170
They're doing these things.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.730
And you are just as
beautiful as anybody else.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:20.760
- Oh my God.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.593
(audience claps)

00:02:21.593 --> 00:02:23.300
Well, congratulations on all the success.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.690
I'm liking your right post now.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.540
And that's not all.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.140
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.960
makers of FriXion the go to erasable pen,

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.870
and The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.730
wanna celebrate those creating fearlessly,

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:33.840
just like you ma'am.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.480
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.726
How's that sound?

00:02:36.726 --> 00:02:37.685
(audience cheers)

00:02:37.685 --> 00:02:38.982
- Oh my God! Thank you!

00:02:38.982 --> 00:02:41.497
- [Kelly] I love that reaction!

